%% Pipeline choices — three orthogonal questions that decide how a pipeline actually runs: who
%% owns it, what triggers it, and where its definition lives. The green node in each row is the
%% choice this module's lab wires (dev-owned CI, triggered on every push, defined in the app's
%% own repo — Pipelines-as-Code).
%% Resized 2026-08-22: was 501x431 intrinsic, rendering 900x774 with text at 1.8x. Root cause: the
%% three subgraphs sat side by side (`flowchart LR` at top level) but each was `direction TB`, so
%% every row's two nodes stacked into a narrow column. Swapped to top-level `flowchart TB` with
%% `direction LR` + `~~~` inside (and between) the subgraphs so each question is one short row.
%% Tuned again 2026-08-22: that fix still stacked OWN/TRIG/PLACE into three rows (900x919 @1.87x,
%% too narrow and too tall). Replaced the `OWN ~~~ TRIG ~~~ PLACE` chain with a fan-out from OWN
%% (`OWN ~~~ TRIG` and `OWN ~~~ PLACE`) so TRIG and PLACE share OWN's next rank instead of stacking
%% one after another — two rows instead of three. No subgraphs, edges into them, or labels changed.
flowchart TB
  subgraph OWN["Who owns it?"]
    direction LR
    O1["dev team — CI only<br/>build · test · package"]:::pick
    O2["platform/DevOps team —<br/>promote to stage · prod"]
    O1 ~~~ O2
  end
  subgraph TRIG["What triggers it?"]
    direction LR
    T1["every push"]:::pick
    T2["nightly · tag · manual"]
    T1 ~~~ T2
  end
  subgraph PLACE["Where does it live?"]
    direction LR
    P1["in the app repo<br/>.tekton/"]:::pick
    P2["a separate<br/>pipelines repo"]
    P1 ~~~ P2
  end
  OWN ~~~ TRIG
  OWN ~~~ PLACE
  classDef pick fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
